P(f"The cleaned data comprised {M['n_records']:,} articles; {pc(M['share_D_le_72'])} were accepted within 72 days. Forensic checks found little heaping of D at multiples of 30 days (ratio {C['forensics']['heaping_ratio_D_multiple_of_30_vs_neighbours']:.2f}), {pc(C['forensics']['share_D_le_7'])} of papers with D ≤ 7 days and an expected weekday pattern. Of {X1rs['n']:,} articles with a Research Square preprint (a self-selected sample), {X1sn['n']:,} were in Springer Nature journals ({X1sn['n_journals']} journals): the median received date was {abs(X1sn['median_delta']):.0f} days before posting, {pc(X1sn['share_received_le_posted_plus_14'],0)} were received no later than 14 days after posting and {pc(X1sn['share_received_gt_posted_plus_90'])} more than 90 days after (Figure 2). Journals whose medians looked fast ({X1fast['n_journals']} journals, {X1fast['n']} articles; median D {X1fast['median_D']:.0f} days) showed a similar paper-weighted pattern ({pc(X1fast['share_received_le_posted_plus_14'],0)} and {pc(X1fast['share_received_gt_posted_plus_90'])}; all publishers), although for the {Z4['n_fast_journals']} Springer Nature journals with fast-looking medians the journal-weighted share within 14 days was {pc(Z4['journal_weighted_le14_fastlooking'],0)}. The pre-set criterion that at least 70% of articles fall within ±14 days of posting was not met ({pc(X1sn['share_abs_le_14'],0)}) because these preprints are posted about two weeks after receipt; the criterion was mis-specified, so the other two statistics are post hoc and show compatibility with, not confirmation of, the received date being the original submission date. Weighting journals equally rather than papers, {pc(Z4['journal_weighted_le14'],0)} of articles were received no later than 14 days after posting and {pc(Z4['journal_weighted_gt90'])} more than 90 days after. The median offset varied with received year (2021–2026: from {min(v for k,v in Z4['median_delta_by_received_year'].items() if k>='2021'):.0f} to {max(v for k,v in Z4['median_delta_by_received_year'].items() if k>='2021'):.0f} days), so the posting lag shifted over time, and a systematic offset of up to 14 days (about 11% of the median D) cannot be excluded at this resolution. For Wiley and Taylor & Francis journals the probe is uninformative (their Research Square preprints are independent postings: median received {X1['ResearchSquare_by_member']['Wiley']['median_delta']:.0f} and {X1['ResearchSquare_by_member']['Taylor & Francis']['median_delta']:.0f} days after posting).")
