P(f"Remedies were evaluated under a strict rule: only earlier cohorts whose targets were complete at the origin were used (origins October 2023, January 2024 and April 2024). There F0 under-covered by {pt(Z2['F0_shortfall']['est'])} points (CI {pt(Z2['F0_shortfall']['lo'])} to {pt(Z2['F0_shortfall']['hi'])}). Quantile-level recalibration R gave {pt(Z2['R_shortfall']['est'])} points (CI {pt(Z2['R_shortfall']['lo'])} to {pt(Z2['R_shortfall']['hi'])}), constant width inflation V (factor {list(Z2['cscale_by_origin'].values())[0]:.3f}) {pt(Z2['V_shortfall']['est'])} ({pt(Z2['V_shortfall']['lo'])} to {pt(Z2['V_shortfall']['hi'])}) and the empirical-Bayes F4 {pt(Z2['F4_shortfall']['est'])} ({pt(Z2['F4_shortfall']['lo'])} to {pt(Z2['F4_shortfall']['hi'])}). All three therefore over-covered; R and V were learned from early origins at which the shortfall was larger ({pt(Z6['origin_means'][0])} to {pt(Z6['origin_means'][2])} points at the three origins used) than at the evaluation origins ({pt(Z6['origin_means'][7])} to {pt(Z6['origin_means'][9])}), which is one plausible reason, and F4 is a wider forecaster without any such map. In absolute terms V reduced the coverage error (1.1 against 1.9 points) while R merely changed its sign. Pinball loss relative to F0 changed by {Z2['R_pinball_minus_F0']['est']:+.4f} for R (CI {Z2['R_pinball_minus_F0']['lo']:+.4f} to {Z2['R_pinball_minus_F0']['hi']:+.4f}), {Z2['V_pinball_minus_F0']['est']:+.4f} for V and {Z2['F4_pinball_minus_F0']['est']:+.4f} for F4; the pooled forecast F2 had near-nominal coverage ({pt(Z2['F2_shortfall']['est'])} points) but {Z2['F2_pinball_minus_F0']['est']:+.3f} higher loss. The learned forecaster L reached nominal coverage ({pt(CM['F10_cov80_minus_nominal']['mean'])} points) at no loss in the first-pass run, but with the same look-ahead labelling and censored 2025 target, and it was trained on one or two cohorts, so this does not show that a learned remedy works. A first-pass recalibration whose labels were not restricted to cohorts complete at the origin (the look-ahead variant) had moved 2024–2025 coverage from {pt(CM['F0_cov80_minus_nominal']['mean'])} to {pt(CM['F9_cov80_minus_nominal']['mean'])} points; because it used information an author would not have, and the 2025 target was censored, we do not treat it as evidence for the remedy. A one-parameter correction learned from earlier cohorts is thus a partial and unstable remedy for average coverage; it is not a recommendation for practice.")
